gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.32bbdc1f2ad531e23b0face28d258eccda3c76c0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 10:13PM MDT until October 24 at 12:15AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River will continue in and around\nthe communities of Conejos and Antonito due to excessive rainfall\nover the previous couple days.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1215 AM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Conejos River, creeks, streams, and other\nlow-lying and flood-prone locations will continue overnight as high\nwater continues to flow downstream. Mandatory evacuations continue\nalong portions of the Conejos River near Antonito. The Conejos\nRiver will continue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier\nrainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1007 PM MDT, local law enforcement reported flooding in the\nAntonito area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Stream gauges on the Conejos River and San Antonio River near\nManassa continue to show rising water.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Conejos, Bountiful and Ortiz.\n- Highway 17 between Antonito and Cumbres Pass remains closed due\nto flooding and debris.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2f53821717ed69a67daec1135eef04172e322143.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2f53821717ed69a67daec1135eef04172e322143.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 5:44PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible although the risk will decrease into the evening as\nstronger showers and thunderstorms diminish.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may exacerbate flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Waves of showers and isolated embedded thunderstorms will\ncontinue into the evening.  Although rainfall will be more\nlimited in coverage, localized amounts of up to 0.5 inches could\ncause additional minor rises in the smaller creeks and\ntributaries.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley with\nthe greatest risk across Conejos County.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T04:46:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 240446 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1046 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain threat will develop over the eastern plains on Saturday into Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks Saturday afternoon and evening. - Mainly dry this upcoming week then another storm possible next weekend. && .UPDATE... Issue","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet